      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "QUINLEE BALE (1) caught the eye when clocking a speedy 34.50 over 600m at The Meadows three back then has hit the frame in both runs since. Rates a top chance if runs up to time three back. MEANINGFUL (2) missed the hat-trick last start when fifth and beaten 6 lengths (35.08) last time at The Meadows. Solid record at the distance winning three races. A forward showing wouldn't surprise. ELITE ONE (5) has a big motor and ideally suited at the longer trips. Was a winner last time (30.19) over 525m at The Meadows in a Grade 5 and is even better suited at the extra journey. Has a strong record at this distance including four wins. Goes well out of this box with a win and three minor placings. Shapes as a top winning chance on latest effort. VICTORY BARRY (8) must be included in calculations.",
